# direnv: pins gh to the personal account for this OSS repo (see genesis)
.envrc

# genesis local control plane runtime state (genesis serve).
#
# A pattern, not an enumeration. This used to list four names
# (.disabled-by-genesis, .orchestrator.lock, .poll-etag, .poll-highwater) and
# genesis serve then started writing a fifth, .trigger-state, which nothing
# ignored — so every local run left a dirty working tree for the next agent to
# read, or to sweep into a commit with `git add -A`.
#
# The convention the framework already follows is what the pattern encodes: a
# dotfile directly under .genesis/ is per-machine runtime state, everything
# tracked here (config.toml, onboarding.md, design/, scripts/) is not a dotfile.
# Pinned by TestGenesisRuntimeStateIsIgnoredByPattern.
#
# An already-tracked file is unaffected by gitignore, and a future .genesis
# dotfile that genuinely belongs in the repo can still be added with `git add -f`.
.genesis/.*
